  "latest_nl_proof": "Fix any real number x. By the definition of the floor function, floor(x) is the greatest integer less than or equal to x; in particular, floor(x) \u2264 x. Subtracting floor(x) from both sides gives x - floor(x) \u2265 0. Since x was arbitrary, this holds for every real number x. Hence, for all real x, 0 \u2264 x - floor(x).",
